<h3>What is BMR?</h3>

Your Basal Metabolic Rate is the energy your body uses at complete rest to
maintain essential functions — breathing, circulation, cell production and
temperature regulation.

<h3>How it is calculated</h3>

This calculator uses the Harris-Benedict equation, which accounts for your
weight, height, age and gender.

<h3>Using your result</h3>

Multiply your BMR by an activity factor to estimate total daily calorie
needs. All five activity levels are shown with your result.
